# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trivy Ignore File
# Location: tooling/.trivyignore
# Scope: IaC config scanning (trivy config)
#
# Policy:
# - Ignore just for False Positive or Temporary Accepted Risk
# - Every Ignore must have reason, owner, and expires
# - Avoid using wildcard/ignore rules
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Format guideline:
# <RULE_ID>[:<PATH_PATTERN>] # owner=<team|person> reason="<why>" expires=YYYY-MM-DD ticket=<id>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXAMPLES (UNCOMMENT ONLY IF NEEDED AND VALIDATED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example: False-positive in test fixtures only
# AVD-AWS-0132:modules/**/tests/** # owner=platform-security reason="Test-only fixture, no deploy path" expires=2026-12-31 ticket=SEC-1421

# Example: Temporary risk acceptance for legacy module path
# AVD-AWS-0089:modules/legacy-*/** # owner=cloud-platform reason="Legacy migration in progress; compensating controls enabled" expires=2026-10-15 ticket=RISK-778

# Example: Ignore in examples only (never in production module root)
# AVD-AWS-0107:modules/**/examples/** # owner=iac-core reason="Example code intentionally minimal; production baselines enforced in real usage" expires=2026-09-30 ticket=SEC-1550

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACTIVE ENTRIES
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intentionally empty by default.
# Add approved exceptions below this line.
